.TH REAC-PW 1 "October 2026" "reac-pw" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reac-pw \- PipeWire-native Roland REAC endpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reac-pw
[\fB\-\-live\fR \fIIFNAME\fR | \fB\-\-pcap\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-role\fR \fImaster\fR|\fIslave\fR|\fItap\fR]
[\fB\-\-rate\fR \fIRATE\fR]
[\fB\-\-tx\fR \fIIFNAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIKEY\fR=\fIVALUE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reac-pw
puts Roland REAC stageboxes on the PipeWire graph. A box plugged into a network port appears as
capture channels for its inputs and playback channels for its outputs, sized and named from what the
box says on the wire.
.PP
Run as the packaged user service, with no arguments, it listens on every Ethernet interface that has
a link, takes each interface that carries REAC frames as a segment, and decides from the wire whether
to be the master or a slave on it. Enable the service once, as the console user:
.PP
.RS
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now reac-pw
.RE
.PP
The daemon refuses to run as root. The package gives it the file capabilities it needs instead:
cap_net_raw, cap_net_admin and cap_sys_nice.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-live " IFNAME"
Capture live from an interface. May be repeated, or given as a comma list, to serve several segments
from one daemon.
.TP
.BI \-\-pcap " FILE"
Replay a REAC capture, for offline testing.
.TP
.BI \-\-role " ROLE"
\fBmaster\fR: drive the handshake and own the clock, and a
stagebox slaves to this machine. \fBslave\fR: an external master drives, and this machine locks to its
cadence and returns its inputs upstream. \fBtap\fR: passive; serve what is heard and transmit nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " RATE"
The REAC sample rate: 44100, 48000 or 96000. A master defaults to 96000; a slave detects the rate from
the wire.
.TP
.BI \-\-tx " IFNAME"
The interface frames are sent on. The default is the interface being served.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
A suffix for the PipeWire node names, so that one master per segment can coexist.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " KEY" = VALUE
Set any tunable by name, at the highest precedence. May be repeated. An unknown key is refused.
.TP
.B \-\-help
List every option and tunable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/reac-pw/reac-pw.conf
The one hand-written override file: a \fB[segment IFNAME]\fR section per interface, with \fBrole =
auto|master|slave|tap\fR and \fBignore = yes\fR. Without it every segment is decided from the wire.
.TP
.I ~/.config/reac-pw/reac-pw.env
Per-user settings, host-wide or per segment.
.PP
Worked examples of both are installed with the package documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR pw-link (1)
.PP
https://github.com/FreeREAC/reac-pw
